'''Baldwin Malcolm Frank''' (born December 5, 1968) is an American former professional [[gridiron football|football]] player who was a [[defensive back]] in the [[World League of American Football]] (WLAF), the [[National Football League]] (NFL), and the [[Canadian Football League]] (CFL). He won two [[Grey Cup]] championships with the [[Edmonton Elks|Edmonton Eskimos]] in 2003 and 2005.<ref>{{cite web|last=Jones|first=Terry|title=Green, Gold & Grey-t?: Eskimos celebrate another Cup|work=Edmonton Sun|publisher=Slam! Sports|date=November 29, 2005|url=http://slam.canoe.com/Slam/Football/CFL/Edmonton/2005/11/29/1328870-sun.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160310152917/http://slam.canoe.com/Slam/Football/CFL/Edmonton/2005/11/29/1328870-sun.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=March 10, 2016|access-date=February 1, 2011}}</ref>
